        "GND",
        "Display_Power_Switch"
      ],
      "observed": "C1 is a 0.1uF/16V capacitor connected between GND and Display_Power_Switch.",
      "expected": "The EPD driver specification table states C1 should be 1 µF/25 V, matching C5/C7/C8/C9/C10.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The display power rail has less intended capacitance, which can affect EPD boost/charge-pump stability and display update behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist deviates from the intended design at the Q2 display power switch: the specified 10 kΩ gate pull-up R2 is absent and replaced by a 1 µF capacitor to +3V3, leaving the gate without a defined off state. C1 also has a value mismatch relative to the stated EPD driver table."
}

